WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.350
The Severn estuary, on the coast of Wales,

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.250
has an enormous tidal range.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.630
In 2010, a government study
looked at five possible schemes.

4
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.430
The biggest was a barrage
from Cardiff to Weston,

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.630
which could make 15.6 terawatt
hours of electricity a year.

6
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.970
Off North Wales, 160 wind turbines
have been turning since 2015.

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.340
The barrage is still a
dashed line on a map.

8
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.130
So why has a dam across the
Severn never been built?

9
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.390
In this mission, you'll compare
tidal barrages and lagoons,

10
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.210
and see how each turns
tides into electricity.

11
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.830
Then you'll weigh up the impacts of
wind and tidal power on this coast.

12
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:46.370
Your mission: find out why the Severn
has never been dammed for power.
